<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Roland on nonpunctual</title><link>https://www.nonpunctual.org/tags/roland/</link><description>Recent content in Roland on nonpunctual</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 01 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.nonpunctual.org/tags/roland/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>10 Ragas To a Disco Beat</title><link>https://www.nonpunctual.org/posts/10-ragas-to-a-disco-beat/</link><pubDate>Fri, 01 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.nonpunctual.org/posts/10-ragas-to-a-disco-beat/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;In 1982, &lt;a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charanjit_Singh_%28musician%29" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;Charanjit Singh&lt;/a&gt; released &lt;a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Synthesizing:_Ten_Ragas_to_a_Disco_Beat" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;&amp;lsquo;Synthesizing: Ten Ragas To a Disco Beat&amp;rsquo;&lt;/a&gt; which is my favorite acid house album. (There are a lot of words in that sentence that don&amp;rsquo;t go together.) It was a marketplace flop from a musician &amp;amp; composer who otherwise had a long &amp;amp; successful career in the Indian 🇮🇳 music &amp;amp; film industries.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;I love talking about &lt;a href="https://www.nonpunctual.org/gear/boss-aw-3/#old-faithful" &gt;flops&lt;/a&gt;. Learning about &amp;amp; talking about &lt;a href="https://www.nonpunctual.org/gear/roland-super-jx-mks-70/#thoughts" &gt;flops&lt;/a&gt; makes me feel better. It gives me hope that so many of the things considered failures or &amp;ldquo;bad&amp;rdquo; often are really just out of phase - ahead or behind the rest of the world at the time of their release or invention.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>nonpunctual.org Gear</title><link>https://www.nonpunctual.org/projects/nonpunctual.org-gear/</link><pubDate>Wed, 01 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.nonpunctual.org/projects/nonpunctual.org-gear/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="overview"&gt;&#10; Overview&#10; &lt;a class="heading-link" href="#overview"&gt;&#10; &lt;i class="fa-solid fa-link" aria-hidden="true" title="Link to heading"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="sr-only"&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;I have some &lt;a href="https://www.nonpunctual.org/gear" &gt;stuff&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="timeline"&gt;&#10; Timeline&#10; &lt;a class="heading-link" href="#timeline"&gt;&#10; &lt;i class="fa-solid fa-link" aria-hidden="true" title="Link to heading"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="sr-only"&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Not like a hoarder. (I suppose this is relative&amp;hellip;) I don&amp;rsquo;t believe I have a &lt;em&gt;problem&lt;/em&gt; (Doesn&amp;rsquo;t everyone who has a problem say that?) If I do have a problem, it started in earnest around 1984-85 when I got my 1st &amp;ldquo;real&amp;rdquo; &lt;a href="https://www.nonpunctual.org/gear/moog-liberation/#pitch" &gt;synthesizer&lt;/a&gt;. So it&amp;rsquo;s an honest, long-standing problem.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Roland SUPER JX MKS-70</title><link>https://www.nonpunctual.org/gear/roland-super-jx-mks-70/</link><pubDate>Wed, 01 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.nonpunctual.org/gear/roland-super-jx-mks-70/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="photos"&gt;&#10; Photos&#10; &lt;a class="heading-link" href="#photos"&gt;&#10; &lt;i class="fa-solid fa-link" aria-hidden="true" title="Link to heading"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="sr-only"&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img src="https://www.nonpunctual.org/images/Roland%20MKS-70.jpg"&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;alt="Roland SUPER JX MKS-70"&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;p&gt;Professional.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&lt;/figcaption&gt;&#10;&lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;br&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="overview"&gt;&#10; Overview&#10; &lt;a class="heading-link" href="#overview"&gt;&#10; &lt;i class="fa-solid fa-link" aria-hidden="true" title="Link to heading"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="sr-only"&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://reverb.com/p/roland-mks-70" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;https://reverb.com/p/roland-mks-70&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.synthmania.com/mks-70_super_jx.htm" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;https://www.synthmania.com/mks-70_super_jx.htm&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.vintagesynth.com/roland/mks-70" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;https://www.vintagesynth.com/roland/mks-70&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;br&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="specification"&gt;&#10; Specification&#10; &lt;a class="heading-link" href="#specification"&gt;&#10; &lt;i class="fa-solid fa-link" aria-hidden="true" title="Link to heading"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="sr-only"&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Basics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;table&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;thead&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;th&gt;Features&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;th&gt;Description&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;/thead&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;tbody&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;Architecture&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;2 sections: (A &amp;amp; B), 2 DCO + 1 VCF + 1 VCA + 2 EG per voice&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;Audio&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;combined mono output + (2) sets of stereo outputs (A &amp;amp; B), 1 for each section&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;Form Factor&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;19&amp;quot; rack mount module of the &lt;a href="https://reverb.com/p/roland-super-jx-10-76-key-polyphonic-synthesizer" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;Roland SUPER JX JX-10 keyboard&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;Polyphony&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;dual 6-voice or 12 voice modes&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;/tbody&gt;&#10;&lt;/table&gt;&#10;&lt;br&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manuals&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>